reator tricks his friend Ben into wielding a supposedly cursed weapon, part of a series of cursed-object content including a cursed book and cursed AirPods. The video is comedic and ends with a humorous exchange about eternal curses.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/JJJeMNRkIVo/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-03T16:01:47.000Z"},{"id":"vzwiZpRfm","title":"Offsite Karaoke","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s-x_bXO7nzA","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/offsite-karaoke-vzwizprfm","summary":"A comedic sketch/video script depicting workplace conflict between developers over code reviews and PR quality, featuring a sprint retrospective gone wrong, a team offsite, and karaoke as the resolution. The content includes sponsored segments for Railway (deployment platform) and CodeRabbit (AI code review tool). The narrative parody touches on common developer frustrations like AI-generated code, slow PRs, and code quality debates.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/s-x_bXO7nzA/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-31T16:52:46.000Z"},{"id":"SLIv03DyQ","title":"Around the Sprint Board","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F1CQHYO7m1w","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/around-the-sprint-board-sliv03dyq","summary":"A satirical piece written in the style of a fantasy sports broadcast ('Around the Sprint Board'), where software engineers at companies like AWS are treated like fantasy sports players. The segment 'analyzes' a fictional AWS senior engineer named Ben Burke, critiquing his low code commit count, PR merges, and a production incident \u2014 all framed as fantasy sports statistics and draft picks. The bit ends with a mention of comparing rookie engineers' stats to Claude Code.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/F1CQHYO7m1w/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-27T16:47:05.000Z"},{"id":"ngcGAMnP5","title":"Fantasy FAANGball","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KIZt9YPAPZo","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/fantasy-faangball-ngcgamnp5","summary":"A satirical comedy sketch that parodies fantasy sports culture by applying it to software engineers at major tech companies (FAANG). Engineers are 'drafted' and evaluated like athletes based on PR counts, code commits, and architecture contributions. The sketch includes mock sports commentary, a fake workplace training video, and a Supabase/Cloudflare sponsor parody, poking fun at developer productivity metrics, tech industry culture, and the absurdity of measuring engineering output.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/KIZt9YPAPZo/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-24T16:44:46.000Z"},{"id":"Go6SrCGff","title":"Blindfolded strangers try to identify the Android user in the room","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MKJ-khXqgLk","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/bro-is-not-beating-the-allegations-go6srcgff","summary":"A humorous social experiment video where strangers try to identify the one Android user among a group of iPhone users, playing on the cultural stereotypes around smartphone brand loyalty.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/MKJ-khXqgLk/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-20T16:22:29.000Z"},{"id":"bnUQf2JkM","title":"screen time limits","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2ozrCNgZPcs","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/screen-time-limits-bnuqf2jkm","summary":"A comedic conversation snippet about screen time limits and increasingly absurd methods people use to curb phone addiction, including math-problem apps and hiring a bouncer to punch them in the face.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2ozrCNgZPcs/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-13T19:42:03.000Z"},{"id":"g05OHTOHM","title":"Paradise Episode 1 | Public Memories","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AS9y-d2BvZU","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/paradise-episode-1-public-memories-g05ohtohm","summary":"A comedic sketch show episode featuring interconnected vignettes: elderly parents setting up futuristic brain-interface devices ('lantern flights') with help from their son, parody ads for Supabase and CodeRabbit, a cooking show satirizing busy tech workers who don't eat, and a storyline where a dad gets a brain virus from scam sites and loses his memories after a factory reset. The humor blends near-future tech satire with relatable internet culture references.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/AS9y-d2BvZU/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-10T20:21:02.000Z"},{"id":"bCEIhGSKZ","title":"Paradise (Trailer) | a new sketch show","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cjEUZ-ChU7A","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/paradise-trailer-a-new-sketch-show-bceihgskz","summary":"A trailer for 'Paradise', a sketch comedy show that parodies workplace developer culture, touching on relatable software engineering experiences like being stuck on Kubernetes, unfair PR review comments, and CAPTCHA frustrations.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/cjEUZ-ChU7A/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-25T20:21:02.000Z"},{"id":"wgIKTd69Z","title":"Data hunters extract embarrassing personal data for AI training","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IU4ByUbDKNc","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/rare-data-hunters-wgiktd69z","summary":"A satirical video sketch depicts 'data hunters' extracting embarrassing personal data from old hard drives to train AI models, highlighting privacy concerns around data collection for machine learning. The piece uses humor to critique aggressive data harvesting practices while being sponsored by Cloudflare, which promotes its cloud infrastructure services including R2 storage, AI deployment tools, and streaming capabilities.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/IU4ByUbDKNc/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":